+      "title": "Two-bond rectangle obstruction to uniform Cardy approximation: draft",
+      "statement": "DRAFT AUTHOR DERIVATION; INDEPENDENT REVIEW BY w416 PENDING. Let delta>0 and take Q_delta=(0,2 delta) x (-delta/2,delta/2), marked at its corners. Its closed-rectangle induced delta Z^2 graph has exactly three vertices and two bonds, so free Bernoulli(1/2) left-to-right crossing probability is exactly 1/4. For horizontal aspect ratio 2, Cardy has cross ratio x=(sqrt(2)-1)^4 and value C(x)=B_x(1/3,1/3)/B(1/3,1/3). Since x<1/32, the beta-integral bounds give C(x)<(8/961)^(1/3)<1/4. Thus the approximation error exceeds 1/4-(8/961)^(1/3)>0 at every delta. This refutes only an unrestricted uniform-domain auxiliary assertion. The relative mesh delta/height(Q_delta)=1; no fixed-domain Cardy limit or C0017 solution is refuted or proved.",
